oot/hand contact, fingers through the handle or required contact hidden from inspection.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"start-pose","views":["start"],"observe":"Working phase starts: hanging with straight arms overhead, body upright, knees on the pad, shoulders reaching up","reject":"Wrong start position, range, grip or support.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"end-pose","views":["end"],"observe":"Working phase ends: body pulled up until the chin is level with the handles, elbows bent sharply and down beside the ribs, chest toward the handles, knees still on the pad","reject":"Wrong endpoint, unintended lockout, torso compensation or shifted fixed hardware.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"mechanical-travel","views":["start","end"],"observe":"Motion: the whole body rises straight up. Lever rotates about its actual pivot; sled/bar stays on rails; cable stays connected along the same route.","reject":"Free-floating handle, cable through body/frame, impossible lever translation or moving camera/chassis.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"critical-alignment","views":["alignment"],"observe":"the top of the pull: chin level with the handles, elbows bent sharply and down beside the ribs, chest up toward the handles, knees on the pad","reject":"Critical contact, joint or pivot obscured; roller in wrong location, incorrect alignment or pose.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"technique","views":["setup","start","end","alignment"],"observe":"Visible technique agrees with: Hang with straight arms but active shoulders: pull them slightly down, away from the ears, before each rep.; Drive the elbows down and back until your chin clears the handles.; Keep the ribs down and the legs still: no kicking or swinging.; Exhale on the way up, inhale on the way down.","reject":"Depiction encourages these authored mistakes: Stepping off the pad before standing on the steps: the platform springs up.; Dropping into the bottom and hanging on relaxed, shrugged shoulders.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"same-actor","views":["setup","start","end","alignment"],"observe":"Same adult proportions and limb lengths; hands have five digits with natural occlusion, thumb opposing fingers around the grip.","reject":"Extra/fused digits or limbs, changed proportions, handle detached from hand or impossible bend.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"house-language","views":["identity","adjustment","setup","start","end","alignment"],"observe":"Ivory ground, thin brown contour, matte graphite frame, cream pads, grey hardware/person, orange only on adjustment controls; one scene.","reject":"Photorealism, glossy render, food props, lettering, logos, arrows, diagram insets or muscle overlays.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"framing","views":["identity","setup","start","end"],"observe":"All required contacts and working mechanism visible; start/end share camera, scale and crop; 8% outer margin.","reject":"Cropped working lever, foot/head, altered crop or contact hidden by frame.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."}],"sourceCorrections":[],"languageVersion":"machine-language-2.0","language":{"version":"machine-language-2.0","policySource":"art/image-requirements.json","policyScope":"Inherit the site''s thin warm contours, muted matte cel shading, ivory ground and no-text/no-arrow rendering lock. Fitness explicitly replaces culinary subject/hand-only framing with a whole adult mannequin and commercial gym equipment. No food props, ingredient rules, manufacturer identity or photorealism.","styleReference":"public/media/illustrations/nigiri/technique-4.webp","styleReferenceRole":"Palette and linework only; never use food geometry as machine geometry.","rendering":"Scientific educational gym illustration in the site''s hand-drawn Japanese-animation visual language. Thin even warm-brown contours, smooth matte two-tone cel shading, no gradients, grain, gloss or photographic texture. Plain warm ivory background edge to edge, one restrained ground shadow. No environment, typography, numbers, logos, arrows, diagrams, borders or insets. One scene and one camera per image.","palette":{"background":"#faf6ef","outline":"#4a3a2a","frame":"#3b3632","upholstery":"#efe6d6","hardware":"#c9c3b8","adjustmentControls":"#b83d0b","actorBase":"#d8cfc3","actorShadow":"#b9ad9e"},"actor":"One neutral adult training mannequin, consistent athletic proportions and scale in all views; smooth faceless head, warm-grey body, no sexual anatomy, hair or clothing changes. Anatomically plausible joints and five digits per hand with natural occlusion, thumb opposing fingers around the grip; no mittens, fused digits or extra limbs. Keep the same limb lengths, handedness, stance and supporting contacts across phases. No painted muscle overlays; muscle maps are a separate asset family.","machineLock":"Preserve the approved machine''s frame silhouette, frame feet, weld topology, pad dimensions, upholstery, pivot positions, rail angle, cable routing, adjustment controls and attachment family. Moving handles, lever arms, sled and cable endpoints move as one physically connected mechanism. Never move fixed pads or invent a second mechanism to accommodate a pose. Use a generic training station, not an unverified branded model.","cameraLock":"Body views use a 50mm-equivalent orthographic-like view with