d contact/joint","requiredViewCount":6,"requiredViews":["identity","adjustment","setup","start","end","alignment"],"checkpoints":[{"id":"frame-identity","views":["identity","setup","start","end"],"observe":"Full fixed chassis: One upright cable tower with a guarded stack, vertical adjustment rail, one height-adjustable locked pulley carriage, cable and interchangeable attachment; stable floor base. Carriage height and attachment vary by the exercise; chassis and cable route remain identical.","reject":"Changed frame feet, extra stack/lever, floating component or cropped load mechanism.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"exercise-configuration","views":["adjustment","setup","start","end"],"observe":"Attachment and hardware: a single cable column with the pulley carriage set LOW, at about knee height, and a single stirrup handle","reject":"Wrong attachment, resistance mechanism, cable routing or rail/pad orientation.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"adjustments","views":["adjustment","setup"],"observe":"Before movement: standing facing away from the column in a split stance, the working arm extended down and behind the body holding the handle, palm forward. The adjustment pin or latch is visibly engaged. Body-relative settings are not universal seat numbers or prescribed kilograms.","reject":"Unlatched adjustment, invented numbered setting/load, pad or grip contradicting the setup.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"setup-contacts","views":["setup","start","end"],"observe":"Supporting contacts and grip: standing facing away from the column in a split stance, the working arm extended down and behind the body holding the handle, palm forward","reject":"Missing pad/foot/hand contact, fingers through the handle or required contact hidden from 