 a guarded stack, vertical adjustment rail, one height-adjustable locked pulley carriage, cable and interchangeable attachment; stable floor base. Carriage height and attachment vary by the exercise; chassis and cable route remain identical.","reject":"Changed frame feet, extra stack/lever, floating component or cropped load mechanism.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"exercise-configuration","views":["adjustment","setup","start","end"],"observe":"Attachment and hardware: a single cable column with the pulley carriage set at the LOWEST position and a single stirrup handle","reject":"Wrong attachment, resistance mechanism, cable routing or rail/pad orientation.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"adjustments","views":["adjustment","setup"],"observe":"Before movement: standing side-on to the low pulley, holding the handle in the far hand so the cable crosses in front of the body; the near hand on the column. The adjustment pin or latch is visibly engaged. Body-relative settings are not universal seat numbers or prescribed kilograms.","reject":"Unlatched adjustment, invented numbered setting/load, pad or grip contradicting the setup.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"setup-contacts","views":["setup","start","end"],"observe":"Supporting contacts and grip: standing side-on to the low pulley, holding the handle in the far hand so the cable crosses in front of the body; the near hand on the column","reject":"Missing pad/foot/hand contact, fingers through the handle or required contact hidden from inspection.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"start-pose","views":["start"],"observe":"Working phase starts: working arm hanging across the front of the hips, elbow softly bent","reject":"Wrong start position, range, grip or support.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"end-pose","views":["end"],"observe":"Working phase ends: working arm raised out to the side to shoulder height, elbow slightly bent and level with the hand","reject":"Wrong endpoint, unintended lockout, torso compensation or shifted fixed hardware.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"mechanical-travel","views":["start","end"],"observe":"Motion: an upward arc out to the side from the front of the hips to shoulder height. Lever rotates about its actual pivot; sled/bar stays on rails; cable stays connected along the same route.","reject":"Free-floating handle, cable through body/frame, impossible lever translation or moving camera/chassis.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"critical-alignment","views":["alignment"],"observe":"Show these critical supporting contacts at the start position: standing side-on to the low pulley, holding the handle in the far hand so the cable crosses in front of the body; the near hand on the column; working arm hanging across the front of the hips, elbow softly bent","reject":"Critical contact, joint or pivot obscured; roller in wrong location, incorrect alignment or pose.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"technique","views":["setup","start","end","alignment"],"observe":"Visible technique agrees with: Soft bend in the elbow, with the elbow leading the hand.; Raise the arm out to the side until it is level with the shoulder.; Keep the shoulder down and the torso still — no leaning.; Pause briefly, then lower for 2–3 s until the hand is by your hip.","reject":"Depiction encourages these authored mistakes: Shrugging the shoulder up to start the rep.; Leaning away from the stack to swing the weight.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"same-actor","views":["setup","start","end","alignment"],"observe":"Same adult proportions and limb lengths; hands have five digits with natural occlusion, thumb opposing fingers around the grip.","reject":"Extra/fused digits or limbs, changed proportions, handle detached from hand or impossible bend.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"house-language","views":["identity","adjustment","setup","start","end","alignment"],"observe":"Ivory ground, thin brown contour, matte graphite frame, cream pads, grey hardware/person, orange only on adjustment controls; one scene.","reject":"Photorealism, glossy render, food props, lettering, logos, arrows, diagram insets or muscle overlays.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"framing","views":["identity","setup","start","end"],"observe":"All required contacts and working mechanism visible; start/end share camera, scale and crop; 8% outer margin.","reject":"Cropped working lever, foot/head, altered crop or contact hidden by frame.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."}],"sourceCorrections":[],"languageVersion":"machine-language-2.0","language":{"version":"machine-language-2.0","policySource":"art/image-requirements.json","policyScope":"Inherit the site''s thin warm contours, muted matte cel shading, ivory ground and no-text/no-arrow rendering lock. Fitness explicitly replaces culinary subject/hand-only framing with a whole adult mannequin and commercial gym equipment. No food props, ingredient rules, manufacturer identity or photorealism.","styleReference":"public/media/illustrations/nigiri/technique-4.webp","styleReferenceRole":"Palette and linework only; nev