 contact/joint","requiredViewCount":6,"requiredViews":["identity","adjustment","setup","start","end","alignment"],"checkpoints":[{"id":"frame-identity","views":["identity","setup","start","end"],"observe":"Full fixed chassis: a seated pin-loaded converging chest press: an upright back pad, an adjustable seat, two independent handle arms that swing forward and inward on angled pivots so the hands meet in front of the chest, a weight stack beside the seat","reject":"Changed frame feet, extra stack/lever, floating component or cropped load mechanism.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"exercise-configuration","views":["adjustment","setup","start","end"],"observe":"Attachment and hardware: a seated pin-loaded converging chest press: an upright back pad, an adjustable seat, two independent handle arms that swing forward and inward on angled pivots so the hands meet in front of the chest, a weight stack beside the seat","reject":"Wrong attachment, resistance mechanism, cable routing or rail/pad orientation.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"adjustments","views":["adjustment","setup"],"observe":"Before movement: seat set so the handles are level with the middle of the chest; feet flat; back and head against the pad. The adjustment pin or latch is visibly engaged. Body-relative settings are not universal seat numbers or prescribed kilograms.","reject":"Unlatched adjustment, invented numbered setting/load, pad or grip contradicting the setup.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"setup-contacts","views":["setup","start","end"],"observe":"Supporting contacts and grip: seat set so the handles are level with the middle of the chest; feet flat; back and head against the pad","reject":"Missing pad/foot/hand contact, fingers through the handle or required contact hidden from inspection.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"start-pose","views":["start"],"observe":"Working phase starts: hands on the handles beside the chest, elbows bent about 90 degrees and slightly below shoulder height","reject":"Wrong start position, range, grip or support.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"end-pose","views":["end"],"observe":"Working phase ends: arms extended forward and inward, hands almost meeting in front of the breastbone, elbows nearly straight","reject":"Wrong endpoint, unintended lockout, torso compensation or shifted fixed hardware.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"mechanical-travel","views":["start","end"],"observe":"Motion: forward and inward in a gentle arc from beside the chest to in front of the breastbone. Lever rotates about its actual pivot; sled/bar stays on rails; cable stays connected along the same route.","reject":"Free-floating handle, cable through body/frame, impossible lever translation or moving camera/chassis.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"critical-alignment","views":["alignment"],"observe":"Show these critical supporting contacts at the start position: seat set so the handles are level with the middle of the chest; feet flat; back and head against the pad; hands on the handles beside the chest, elbows bent about 90 degrees and slightly below shoulder height","reject":"Critical contact, joint or pivot obscured; roller in wrong location, incorrect alignment or pose.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"technique","views":["setup","start","end","alignment"],"observe":"Visible technique agrees with: Set the shoulder blades back and down before you push the handles off their stops.; Press both handles at the same speed; the arcs meet in front of your lower chest.; Elbows 45–60° from your sides; let them follow the converging path instead of flaring.; Breathe out through the press and stop just short of lockout.","reject":"Depiction encourages these authored mistakes: Seat too low, so the press starts near the shoulders and the elbows ride up.; Letting the handles drift behind the chest at the bottom — a stretch the shoulder capsule pays for.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"same-actor","views":["setup","start","end","alignment"],"observe":"Same adult proportions and limb lengths; hands have five digits with natural occlusion, thumb opposing fingers around the grip.","reject":"Extra/fused digits or limbs, changed proportions, handle detached from hand or impossible bend.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"house-language","views":["identity","adjustment","setup","start","end","alignment"],"observe":"Ivory ground, thin brown contour, matte graphite frame, cream pads, grey hardware/person, orange only on adjustment controls; one scene.","reject":"Photorealism, glossy render, food props, lettering, logos, arrows, diagram insets or muscle overlays.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"framing","views":["identity","setup","start","end"],"observe":"All required contacts and working mechanism visible; start/end share camera, scale and crop; 8% outer margin.","reject":"Cropped working lever, foot/head, altered crop or contact hidden by frame.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."}],"sourceCorrections":[],"languageVersion":"machine-language-2.0","language":{"version":"machine-language-2.0","policySource":"art