evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"end-pose","views":["end"],"observe":"Working phase ends: bar pulled down IN FRONT of the face to the top of the chest at collarbone height (never behind the neck), elbows pointing down and slightly back beside the ribs, forearms vertical under the bar, chest lifted toward the bar; the torso keeps the same slight lean and the thighs stay under the rollers","reject":"Wrong endpoint, unintended lockout, torso compensation or shifted fixed hardware.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"mechanical-travel","views":["start","end"],"observe":"Motion: straight down in front of the face from overhead to the upper chest. Lever rotates about its actual pivot; sled/bar stays on rails; cable stays connected along the same route.","reject":"Free-floating handle, cable through body/frame, impossible lever translation or moving camera/chassis.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"critical-alignment","views":["alignment"],"observe":"the bottom of the pull: bar at the upper chest, elbows down beside the ribs and slightly behind the torso, forearms vertical under the bar, chest up, torso leaning back only about 10 to 15 degrees, thighs under the rollers","reject":"Critical contact, joint or pivot obscured; roller in wrong location, incorrect alignment or pose.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"technique","views":["setup","start","end","alignment"],"observe":"Visible technique agrees with: Sit tall with the chest up and a slight backward lean; keep that torso angle for the whole set.; Start each rep by pulling the shoulder blades down, then drive the elbows down to your sides.; Pull the bar in front of your face to the top of your chest; the elbows finish