 camera looks at the mannequin''s left side at exactly 90 degrees to the direction it faces, so the mannequin is seen in profile facing the right side of the picture, with one arm and one leg in front and the other mostly hidden behind them; never a front, back or three-quarter view","alignmentCamera":"close side view of the stated contact/joint","requiredViewCount":6,"requiredViews":["identity","adjustment","setup","start","end","alignment"],"checkpoints":[{"id":"frame-identity","views":["identity","setup","start","end"],"observe":"Full fixed chassis: a seated pin-loaded lower back machine: a seat with a foot platform, thigh and hip pads that lock the pelvis, a padded roller across the upper back on a lever arm pivoting at the level of the lower back, a weight stack","reject":"Changed frame feet, extra stack/lever, floating component or cropped load mechanism.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"exercise-configuration","views":["adjustment","setup","start","end"],"observe":"Attachment and hardware: a seated pin-loaded lower back machine: a seat with a foot platform, thigh and hip pads that lock the pelvis, a padded roller across the upper back on a lever arm pivoting at the level of the lower back, a weight stack","reject":"Wrong attachment, resistance mechanism, cable routing or rail/pad orientation.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"adjustments","views":["adjustment","setup"],"observe":"Before movement: seat set so the machine''s pivot lines up with the lower back at navel height; feet on the platform, thigh pads locked; upper back against the roller, arms crossed on the chest. The adjustment pin or latch is visibly engaged. Body-relative settings are not universal seat numbers or prescribed kilograms.","reject":"Unlatched adjustment, invented numbered setting/load, pad or grip contradicting the setup.","evidenc