bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"critical-alignment","views":["alignment"],"observe":"the forward position: torso leaning forward about 40 degrees against the roller, pelvis locked by the pads, feet flat on the platform, arms crossed on the chest","reject":"Critical contact, joint or pivot obscured; roller in wrong location, incorrect alignment or pose.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"technique","views":["setup","start","end","alignment"],"observe":"Visible technique agrees with: Lock the pelvis: press the feet into the footrest and the thighs into the pads so the lower back, not the hips, does the work.; Cross your arms on your chest or hold the handles lightly; don''t pull with them.; Extend the trunk back smoothly until you are upright or just past it, no further.; Move slowly: about 2 s back and 3–4 s forward, with no bounce at either end.","reject":"Depiction encourages these authored mistakes: Throwing the trunk back with momentum and slamming into the end of the range.; Arching hard at the end: finish upright, not hyperextended.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"same-actor","views":["setup","start","end","alignment"],"observe":"Same adult proportions and limb lengths; hands have five digits with natural occlusion, thumb opposing fingers around the grip.","reject":"Extra/fused digits or limbs, changed proportions, handle detached from hand or impossible bend.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"house-language","views":["identity","adjustment","setup","start","end","alignment"],"observe":"Ivory ground, thin brown contour, matte graphite frame, cream pads, grey hardware/person, orange only on adjustment controls; one scene.","reject":"Photorealism, glossy render, food props, lettering, logos, arrows, dia