nt about 90 degrees and just below shoulder height, upper arms level with the back pad, chest up, back and head on the pad","alignmentPhase":"hardest-point","camera":"three-quarter front view: the camera stands in front of the mannequin and about 45 degrees to its left, at chest height, so the chest, both arms and the handles are all visible","alignmentCamera":"close side view of the stated contact/joint","requiredViewCount":6,"requiredViews":["identity","adjustment","setup","start","end","alignment"],"checkpoints":[{"id":"frame-identity","views":["identity","setup","start","end"],"observe":"Full fixed chassis: a seated pin-loaded chest press: an upright padded back rest, an adjustable seat, two lever arms (one on each side of the seat, pivoting high on the frame behind the shoulders) that each end in a horizontal handle beside the chest and swing forward with the hands, and a weight stack with a selector pin standing behind the seat; nothing crosses in front of the chest","reject":"Changed frame feet, extra stack/lever, floating component or cropped load mechanism.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"exercise-configuration","views":["adjustment","setup","start","end"],"observe":"Attachment and hardware: a seated pin-loaded chest press: an upright padded back rest, an adjustable seat, two lever arms (one on each side of the seat, pivoting high on the frame behind the shoulders) that each end in a horizontal handle beside the chest and swing forward with the hands, and a weight stack with a selector pin standing behind the seat; nothing crosses in front of the chest","reject":"Wrong attachment, resistance mechanism, cable routing or rail/pad orientation.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"adjustments","views":["adjustment","setup"],"observe":"Before movement: seat height set so the handles are level with the middle of the chest; feet flat on the floor; hips, upper back and head against the back pad; a full grip on the horizontal handles with straight wrists. The adjustment pin or latch is visibly engaged. Body-relative settings are not universal seat numbers or prescribed kilograms.","reject":"Unlatched adjustment, invented numbered setting/load, pad or grip contradicting the setup.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"setup-contacts","views":["setup","start","end"],"observe":"Supporting contacts and grip: seat height set so the handles are level with the middle of the chest; feet flat on the floor; hips, upper back and head against the back pad; a full grip on the horizontal handles with straight wrists","reject":"Missing pad/foot/hand contact, fingers through the handle or required contact hidden from inspection.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"start-pose","views":["start"],"observe":"Working phase starts: hands on the handles beside the chest, elbows bent about 90 degrees and slightly below shoulder height, upper arms about 45 degrees out from the torso, chest up, shoulder blades back against the pad","reject":"Wrong start position, range, grip or support.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"end-pose","views":["end"],"observe":"Working phase ends: arms extended straight forward, handles pushed away to arm''s length at mid-chest height, elbows almost straight but not locked, shoulder blades and head still on the pad","reject":"Wrong endpoint, unintended lockout, torso compensation or shifted fixed hardware.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"mechanical-travel","views":["start","end"],"observe":"Motion: from the handles beside the chest straight forward to arm''s length. Lever rotates about its actual pivot; sled/bar stays on rails; cable stays connected along the same route.","reject":"Free-floating handle, cable through body/frame, impossible lever translation or moving camera/chassis.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"critical-alignment","views":["alignment"],"observe":"the bottom of the press: handles beside the middle of the chest, elbows bent about 90 degrees and just below shoulder height, upper arms level with the back pad, chest up, back and head on the pad","reject":"Critical contact, joint or pivot obscured; roller in wrong location, incorrect alignment or pose.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"technique","views":["setup","start","end","alignment"],"observe":"Visible technique agrees with: Pull your shoulder blades back and down into the pad before the first rep, and keep them there.; Grip with straight wrists in line with the forearms; take the vertical (neutral) handles if the machine has them.; Keep the elbows about 45–60° from your sides, a little below shoulder height.; Breathe out and press smoothly until the arms are almost straight — stop just short of locking out.","reject":"Depiction encourages these authored mistakes: Seat too low: the elbows drift up toward the ears and the front of the shoulder takes the load.; Handles set too deep, so every rep starts behind the chest and overstretches the front of the shoulder.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"same-actor","views":["setup","start","end","alignment"],"observe":"Same adult proportions and limb lengths; hands have five digits with natural occlusion, thumb opposing fingers around the grip.","reject":"Extra/fused digits or limbs, changed proportions, handle detached from hand or impossible bend.","evidence":"Record an observation and 