rking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"setup-contacts","views":["setup","start","end"],"observe":"Supporting contacts and grip: seat set so the handles are at mid-chest height and the shoulders level with the arms'' pivots; back and head against the pad; hands on the vertical handles, elbows softly bent","reject":"Missing pad/foot/hand contact, fingers through the handle or required contact hidden from inspection.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"start-pose","views":["start"],"observe":"Working phase starts: arms open wide to the sides at chest height, elbows softly bent and level with the back pad, a stretch across the chest","reject":"Wrong start position, range, grip or support.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"end-pose","views":["end"],"observe":"Working phase ends: arms swept forward together so the handles nearly touch in front of the chest, elbow bend unchanged, back still on the pad","reject":"Wrong endpoint, unintended lockout, torso compensation or shifted fixed hardware.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"mechanical-travel","views":["start","end"],"observe":"Motion: a curved arrow just above the hand on the right of the picture, starting at that open hand and curving inward toward the middle of the chest, its head pointing at the breastbone. Lever rotates about its actual pivot; sled/bar stays on rails; cable stays connected along the same route.","reject":"Free-floating handle, cable through body/frame, impossible lever translation or moving camera/chassis.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"critical-alignment","views":["alignment"],"observe":"the open, stretched position: upper arms at chest height and in line with the back pad (not behind