ontact/joint","requiredViewCount":6,"requiredViews":["identity","adjustment","setup","start","end","alignment"],"checkpoints":[{"id":"frame-identity","views":["identity","setup","start","end"],"observe":"Full fixed chassis: a plate-loaded iso-lateral chest press: a heavy steel frame with a slightly reclined back pad and a seat, two independent lever arms with vertical handles that pivot from above and behind, round weight plates on a horn on each lever arm, no weight stack","reject":"Changed frame feet, extra stack/lever, floating component or cropped load mechanism.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"exercise-configuration","views":["adjustment","setup","start","end"],"observe":"Attachment and hardware: a plate-loaded iso-lateral chest press: a heavy steel frame with a slightly reclined back pad and a seat, two independent lever arms with vertical handles that pivot from above and behind, round weight plates on a horn on each lever arm, no weight stack","reject":"Wrong attachment, resistance mechanism, cable routing or rail/pad orientation.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"adjustments","views":["adjustment","setup"],"observe":"Before movement: seat set so the handles are level with the middle of the chest; feet flat; back and head on the pad; neutral grip on the vertical handles. The adjustment pin or latch is visibly engaged. Body-relative settings are not universal seat numbers or prescribed kilograms.","reject":"Unlatched adjustment, invented numbered setting/load, pad or grip contradicting the setup.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"setup-contacts","views":["setup","start","end"],"observe":"Supporting contacts and grip: seat set so the handles are level with the middle of the chest; feet flat; back and head on the pad; neutral grip on the vertical handles","reject":"Missing pad/foot/hand contact, fingers through the handle or required contact hidden from inspection.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"start-pose","views":["start"],"observe":"Working phase starts: hands on the handles beside the chest, elbows bent about 90 degrees","reject":"Wrong start position, range, grip or support.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"end-pose","views":["end"],"observe":"Working phase ends: both arms pressed forward to almost straight, the lever arms swung forward","reject":"Wrong endpoint, unintended lockout, torso compensation or shifted fixed hardware.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"mechanical-travel","views":["start","end"],"observe":"Motion: forward and slightly downward in an arc from beside the chest to arm''s length. Lever rotates about its actual pivot; sled/bar stays on rails; cable stays connected along the same route.","reject":"Free-floating handle, cable through body/frame, impossible lever translation or moving camera/chassis.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"critical-alignment","views":["alignment"],"observe":"Show these critical supporting contacts at the start position: seat set so the handles are level with the middle of the chest; feet flat; back and head on the pad; neutral grip on the vertical handles; hands on the handles beside the chest, elbows bent about 90 degrees","reject":"Critical contact, joint or pivot obscured; roller in wrong location, incorrect alignment or pose.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"technique","views":["setup","start","end","alignment"],"observe":"Visible technique agrees wi