r or dumbbells and their path are all visible","alignmentCamera":"close side view of the stated contact/joint","requiredViewCount":6,"requiredViews":["identity","adjustment","setup","start","end","alignment"],"checkpoints":[{"id":"frame-identity","views":["identity","setup","start","end"],"observe":"Full fixed chassis: One Smith rack with two parallel vertical guide rails and one bar sliding on both. Paired hooks and adjustable safety stops engage the frame; plate sleeves sit outside the bearings. Same rack across exercises. A removable adjustable bench is present for presses and absent for squats.","reject":"Changed frame feet, extra stack/lever, floating component or cropped load mechanism.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"exercise-configuration","views":["adjustment","setup","start","end"],"observe":"Attachment and hardware: a Smith machine: a barbell fixed on two vertical steel guide rails inside a tall frame, with rack hooks and adjustable safety stops, and a flat bench placed inside it so the bar comes down over the middle of the chest","reject":"Wrong attachment, resistance mechanism, cable routing or rail/pad orientation.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"adjustments","views":["adjustment","setup"],"observe":"Before movement: lying on the flat bench inside the Smith machine, eyes under the bar, feet flat on the floor, shoulder blades pulled back; hands on the bar a little wider than the shoulders. The adjustment pin or latch is visibly engaged. Body-relative settings are not universal seat numbers or prescribed kilograms.","reject":"Unlatched adjustment, invented numbered setting/load, pad or grip contradicting the setup.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"setup-contacts","views":["setup","start","end"],"observe":"Supporting contacts and grip: lying on the flat bench inside the Smith machine, eyes under the bar, feet flat on the floor, shoulder blades pulled back; hands on the bar a little wider than the shoulders","reject":"Missing pad/foot/hand contact, fingers through the handle or required contact hidden from inspection.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"start-pose","views":["start"],"observe":"Working phase starts: bar lowered to touch the middle of the chest, forearms vertical, elbows about 45 to 60 degrees out from the torso","reject":"Wrong start position, range, grip or support.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"end-pose","views":["end"],"observe":"Working phase ends: bar pressed straight up along the rails to arm''s length above the chest, elbows almost straight","reject":"Wrong endpoint, unintended lockout, torso compensation or shifted fixed hardware.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"mechanical-travel","views":["start","end"],"observe":"Motion: straight up along the guide rails from the chest to arm''s length. Lever rotates about its actual pivot; sled/bar stays on rails; cable stays connected along the same route.","reject":"Free-floating handle, cable through body/frame, impossible lever translation or moving camera/chassis.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"critical-alignment","views":["alignment"],"observe":"Show these critical supporting contacts at the start position: lying on the flat bench inside the Smith machine, eyes under the bar, feet flat on the floor, shoulder blades pulled back; hands on the bar a little wider than the shoulders; bar lowered to touch the middle of the chest, forearms vertical, elbows about 45 to 60 degrees out from the torso","reject":"Critical contact, joint or pivot obscured; roller in wrong location, incorrect alignment or pose.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"technique","views":["setup","start","end","alignment"],"observe":"Visible technique agrees with: Shoulder blades squeezed together and down, feet flat, small natural arch.; Unrack by rotating the hooks off with straight arms over your shoulders.; Lower for 2–3 s to the lower chest with forearms vertical and elbows 45–70° from your sides.; Touch lightly — no bounce — then breathe out and press straight up.","reject":"Depiction encourages these authored mistakes: Bench in the wrong spot, so the fixed bar lands on the neck or belly instead of the lower chest.; No safety stops set — the guided bar still pins you if you fail.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"same-actor","views":["setup","start","end","alignment"],"observe":"Same adult proportions and limb lengths; hands have five digits with natural occlusion, thumb opposing fingers around the grip.","reject":"Extra/fused digits or limbs, changed proportions, handle detached from hand or impossible bend.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"house-language","views":["identity","adjustment","setup","start","end","alignment"],"observe":"Ivory ground, thin brown contour, matte graphite frame, cream pads, grey hardware/person, orange only on adjustment controls; one scene.","reject":"Photorealism, glossy render, food props, lettering, logos, arrows, diagram insets or muscle overlays.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"framing","views":["identity","setup","start","end"],"observe":"All required contacts and working mechanism visible; start/end share camera, scale and crop; 8% outer margin.","rejec