start-contact-check","camera":"pure side (profile) view: the camera looks at the mannequin''s left side at exactly 90 degrees to the direction it faces, so the mannequin is seen in profile facing the right side of the picture, with one arm and one leg in front and the other mostly hidden behind them; never a front, back or three-quarter view","alignmentCamera":"close side view of the stated contact/joint","requiredViewCount":6,"requiredViews":["identity","adjustment","setup","start","end","alignment"],"checkpoints":[{"id":"frame-identity","views":["identity","setup","start","end"],"observe":"Full fixed chassis: a seated pin-loaded vertical traction machine: a seat with padded knee rollers on a short post at the front end of the seat, resting on top of the thighs just behind the knees (in a profile view: a round pad seen end-on, sitting on top of the thigh near the knee, never behind the hips), two independent handle arms above the head that pull down in an arc (no bar and no cable at the hands), a weight stack","reject":"Changed frame feet, extra stack/lever, floating component or cropped load mechanism.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"exercise-configuration","views":["adjustment","setup","start","end"],"observe":"Attachment and hardware: a seated pin-loaded vertical traction machine: a seat with padded knee rollers on a short post at the front end of the seat, resting on top of the thighs just behind the knees (in a profile view: a round pad seen end-on, sitting on top of the thigh near the knee, never behind the hips), two independent handle arms above the head that pull down in an arc (no bar and no cable at the hands), a weight stack","reject":"Wrong attachment, resistance mechanism, cable routing or rail/pad orientation.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"adjustments","views":["adjustment","setup"],"observe":"Before movement: seat set so the thighs fit snugly under the pads and the handles are just reachable with straight arms; feet flat. The adjustment pin or latch is visibly engaged. Body-relative settings are not universal seat numbers or prescribed kilograms.","reject":"Unlatched adjustment, invented numbered setting/load, pad or grip contradicting the setup.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"setup-contacts","views":["setup","start","end"],"observe":"Supporting contacts and grip: seat set so the thighs fit snugly under the pads and the handles are just reachable with straight arms; feet flat","reject":"Missing pad/foot/hand contact, fingers through the handle or required contact hidden from inspection.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"start-pose","views":["start"],"observe":"Working phase starts: arms extended up gripping the handles, shoulders reaching up, torso upright","reject":"Wrong start position, range, grip or support.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"end-pose","views":["end"],"observe":"Working phase ends: handles pulled down to the shoulders, elbows down beside the ribs and slightly back, chest up","reject":"Wrong endpoint, unintended lockout, torso compensation or shifted fixed hardware.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"mechanical-travel","views":["start","end"],"observe":"Motion: down and slightly back in an arc from overhead to the shoulders. Lever rotates about its actual pivot; sled/bar stays on rails; cable stays connected along the same route.","reject":"Free-floating handle, cable through body/frame, impossible lever translation or moving camera/chassis.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"critical-alignment","views":["alignment"],"observe":"Show these critical supporting contacts at the start position: seat set so the thighs fit snugly under the pads and the handles are just reachable with straight arms; feet flat; arms extended up gripping the handles, shoulders reaching up, torso upright","reject":"Critical contact, joint or pivot obscured; roller in wrong location, incorrect alignment or pose.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"technique","views":["setup","start","end","alignment"],"observe":"Visible technique agrees with: Start every rep by drawing the shoulder blades down, then drive the elbows down toward your ribs.; Pull until the handles reach upper-chest level, elbows close to your sides.; Keep the chest up and the torso still; only the arms and shoulder blades move.; Exhale as you pull, inhale as the handles rise.","reject":"Depiction encourages these authored mistakes: Shrugging the shoulders toward the ears at the bottom of the pull.; Leaning far back and turning the pulldown into a row.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"same-actor","views":["setup","start","end","alignment"],"observe":"Same adult proportions and limb lengths; hands have five digits with natural occlusion, thumb opposing fingers around the grip.","reject":"Extra/fused digits or limbs, changed proportions, handle detached from hand or impossible bend.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"house-language","views":["identity","adjustment","setup","start","end","alignment"],"observe":"Ivory ground, thin brown contour, matte graphite frame, cream pads, grey hardware/person, orange only on adjustment controls; one scene.","reject":"Photorealism, glossy render, food props, lettering, logos, arrows, diagram insets or muscle overlays.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."},{"id":"framing","views":["identity","setup","start","end"],"observe":"All required contacts and working mechanism visible; start/end share camera, scale and crop; 8% outer margin.","reject":"Cropped working lever, foot/head, altered crop or contact hidden by frame.","evidence":"Record an observation and normalized bounding box marking the relevant component/contact."}],"sourceCorrections":[],"languageVersion":"machine-language-2.0","language":{"version":"machine-language-2.0","policySource":"art/image-requirements.json","policyScope":"Inherit the site''s thin warm contours, muted matte cel shading, ivory ground and no-text/no-arrow rendering lock. Fitness explicitly replaces culinary subject/hand-only framing with a whole adult mannequin and commercial gym equipment. No food props, ingredient rules, manufacturer identity or photorealism.","styleReference":"public/media/illustrations/nigiri/technique-4.webp","styleReferenceRole":"Palette and linework only; never use food geometry as machine geometry.","rendering":"Scientific educational gym illustration in the site''s hand-drawn Japanese-animation visual language. Thin even warm-brown contours, smooth matte two-tone cel shading, no gradients, grain, gloss or photographic texture. Plain warm ivory background edge to edge, one restrained ground shadow. No environment, typography, numbers, logos, arrows, diagrams, borders or insets. One scene and one camera per image.","palette":{"background":"#faf6ef","outline":"#4a3a2a","frame":"#3b3632","upholstery":"#efe6d6","hardware":"#c9c3b8","adjustmentControls":"#b83d0b","actorBase":"#d8cfc3","actorShadow":"#b9ad9e"},"actor":"One neutral adult training mannequin, consistent athletic proportions and scale in all views; smooth faceless head, warm-grey body, no sexual anatomy, hair or clothing changes. Anatomically plausible joints and five digits per hand with natural occlusion, thumb opposing fingers around the grip; no mittens, fused digits or extra limbs. Keep the same limb lengths, handedness, stance and supporting contacts across phases. No painted muscle overlays; muscle maps are a separate asset family.","machineLock":"Preserve the approved machine''s frame silhouette, frame feet, weld topology, pad dimensions, upholstery, pivot positions, rail angle, cable routing, adjustment controls and attachment family. Moving handles, lever arms, sled and cable endpoints move as one physically connected mechanism. Never move fixed pads or invent a second mechanism to accommodate a pose. Use a generic training station, not an unverified branded model.","cameraLock":"Body views use a 50mm-equivalent orthographic-like view without wide-angle distortion, camera level, same camera/scale/crop across setup, start and end; adult and full working mechanism visible with 8% outer margin. Changing camera is permitted only for the named adjustment/alignment detail views. Camera settings are prompt constraints, not OpenAI API parameters.","api":{"model":"gpt-image-2-2026-04-21","n":1,"size":"1536x1024","quality":"high","background":"opaque","output_format":"png","moderation":"auto"},"requiredViews":["identity","adjustment","setup","start","end","alignment"],"review":{"initialStatus":"unreviewed","requiredEvidence":["reviewer","reviewedAt","imageSha256","promptSha256","actualModel","requestId","allCheckpointDecisions","referenceAssetHashes"],"checkpointEvidence":"Each checkpoint needs an explicit pass/fail, an observation, and at least one normalized bounding box marking the relevant part. Inspect at original resolution and at the delivered thumbnail size. Any failed, missing or hidden required contact blocks approval.","nonDeterminism":"A model snapshot and exact prompts improve traceability; neither seeds nor deterministic image reproduction are promised. No seed or input_fidelity parameter is sent. Actual requests/responses, reference hashes and output hashes must be recorded."},"machineNames":{"single-cable-tower":{"en":"Adjustable cable tower","ru":"Регулируемая блочная стойка"},"dual-cable-crossover":{"en":"Dual cable crossover","ru":"Двойной кроссовер"},"smith-vertical-rack":{"en":"Vertical Smith rack","ru":"Вертикальная машина Смита"},"assisted-dip-chin-station":{"en":"Assisted dip and pull-up station","ru":"Гравитрон для подтягиваний и отжиманий"},"seated-lat-pulldown":{"en":"Lat pulldown station","ru":"Станция вертикальной тяги"},"reversible-pec-rear-delt":{"en":"Pec deck and rear delt machine","ru":"Бабочка и обратная бабочка"},"sled-leg-press-45":{"en":"45-degree sled leg press","ru":"Жим ногами под 45 градусов"}}},"sourceFiles":{"art/fitness/machines/language.json":"9a8cbf68432fc776c788810ea547fca92cb4764cae4e3062c8735a61e4005a7f","art/fitness/machines/specs.json":"47b9b76a1335bbdece7daffcd90b3ab99e15d69241994e7f5e5d483614a4d32e","art/fitness/scenes.json":"189eae0d20c4e976cba552002f00faacad12e39e01a7ec8a26b33cfc718d7e1a","content/fitness/exercises.json":"f62386fe9a23173ba7ed1c3c0d6369be24c9546faa59adf16c66766f2b708827","content/fitness/registry.json":"042300db890e36bdba76819e657a2e93c44f574ad665672ecab09c2866416902","content/fitness/images.json":"e1d79926f4d5033a082f930c7e06ded96d42a8444948cf57ae284f82097db907","art/image-requirements.json":"e70cee64fe164ceba4ba830ceaa8912b5e032bd9e43bd479807eaed0ac6e04bf","src/lib/fitness/catalog-core.mjs":"2584a46c857c0dfe8ca1a8895ca19823fe9b0dcbeb048ba28ee3429acea7c53a","content/fitness/templates.json":"332095547251c2a92d855800ca8ff11bb4fdd6f4632b2f43f1b045533db385c9","scripts/fitness-machine-specs.mjs":"62206120760f0171307ede6e4366c0431085ae66d30e03a4cc1ac6fc9effa131","scripts/fitness-catalog-seed.mjs":"9592fe211b8c420583ebd3c511a6764dae84ceab0fe2fcec460602a758bfba81","public/media/illustrations/nigiri/technique-4.webp":"54f3180cee97ed785cba0c1c161fd60952ece2f8e0edf98eca5f105de0f199af"},"requests":[{"id":"vertical-traction/identity","view":"identity","endpoint